      "hasMediaInOriginal": true,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "—❗️🇸🇦/🇾🇪 Southern Taizz front, Yemen, latest map update:\n\nAnsarallah (the Houthis) have managed to capture Jabal Rasin and Al-Damdam in the direction of Al-Turbah and the Taizz–Aden road.\n\nAnsarallah have also captured Al-Aswad, Al-Aghbirah, Manan, Al-Dharifah, and Uqbah Al-Mansourah on the border between the Taizz–Lahij Governorates.\n\nThey have consolidated their hold over Al-Akkad (Bireen direction) and Al-Ajram (towards Safiya junction), squeezing towards the Taizz–Aden road on all sides from the west.\n\nIn my estimation (which is rather conservative) it will take a maximum of another 1-2 weeks before the last road into Taizz is cut off by Ansarallah, fully encircling the city.\n\n@Middle_East_Spectator",
